From: CARGT <engineering@cargt.com>
Subject: [PATCH] resize-helper: fsck each filesystem before resizing it

The direct-resize2fs fallback path (taken when systemd-growfs isn't
available) runs resize2fs against every GPT-partitioned ext4 device it
finds, with no fsck first. Growing an unverified filesystem produced
severe ext4 metadata corruption on affected units (garbage
i_size/i_blocks, impossible timestamps, orphaned inodes) when this same
pattern was found in a separate first-boot resize script -- fsck each
device immediately before resizing it here too.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not sent upstream]

--- a/resize-helper
+++ b/resize-helper
@@ -67,6 +67,7 @@
         if [ -e /dev/${device} ]; then
             if [ "$PART_TABLE_TYPE" = "gpt" ]; then
                 echo "Resize /dev/${device}"
+                e2fsck -f -y -c -C 0 "/dev/${device}"
                 ${RESIZE2FS} "/dev/${device}"
             fi
         fi
